Overview:
  The Leaderboard pattern provides ranked player lists with multiple
  scopes (global, friends, regional, time-window) and supports both
  real-time top-N queries and full pagination. It separates the write
  model (immutable point events) from the read model (materialized
  leaderboard views) and uses caching strategically to handle high
  read traffic without overwhelming the datastore.

Rules:

  [LB1] Leaderboard read and write models MUST be separated (CQRS).

  [LB2] Real-time leaderboards MUST use sorted-set datastores (Redis ZSET)
        or equivalent.

  [LB3] Full leaderboards MUST be batch-recalculated asynchronously, not
        computed on-demand.

  [LB4] Tie-breaking MUST be deterministic and explicit (secondary sort key).

  [LB5] Leaderboard scopes MUST be configurable: global, friends, regional,
        time-window, custom.

  [LB6] Top-N queries MUST be cached with short TTL (30s-5m).

  [LB7] Deep pagination MUST use seek-based approach, not OFFSET.

  [LB8] Historical/seasonal leaderboards MUST be snapshotted, not recomputed.

  [LB9] Leaderboard updates MUST be idempotent and handle out-of-order events.

  [LB10] User rank queries MUST be O(log N) or better.

Architecture:

  LeaderboardSystem:
    owns:
      - Write model: point event ingestion
      - Read model: materialized leaderboard views
      - Cache layer: hot leaderboard slices
      - Snapshot service: seasonal/historical views
      - Pagination service: seek-based deep navigation

    api:
      - getTopN(scope, n, offset) -> {entries, total, has_more}
      - getUserRank(userId, scope) -> {rank, score, total}
      - getAroundUser(userId, scope, window) -> {entries}
      - snapshot(scope, label) -> snapshot_id
      - rebuild(scope) -> void

    deps:
      - event-store (immutable point events)
      - cache (Redis sorted sets)
      - db (materialized views, snapshots)
      - rule-engine (point validation)

Scopes:
  global:
    description: All users ranked by total points
    dimensions:
      - all_time (default)
      - season_{id}
      - year_{yyyy}
    cache_ttl: 5m (top 1000), 1h (ranks beyond 1000)
  friends:
    description: User's friends ranked by points
    dimensions:
      - all_time
      - season_{id}
    cache_ttl: 2m (per user)
    invalidation: on friend add/remove
  regional:
    description: Users in same region/country ranked
    dimensions:
      - all_time
      - season_{id}
    cache_ttl: 5m
  time_window:
    description: Points earned within time window
    dimensions:
      - daily (today, yesterday)
      - weekly (this week, last week)
      - monthly (this month, last month)
    cache_ttl: 1m
  custom:
    description: Arbitrary filter combination
    dimensions:
      - segment_{id}
      - level_{range}
      - achievement_{id}
    cache_ttl: configurable

TieBreaking:
  primary: score (descending)
  secondary: first_achieved_at (ascending — earlier unlock wins)
  tertiary: auid (ascending — deterministic, no bias)

WriteModel:
  PointEvent:
    event_id: string
    user_id: string
    score_delta: number
    reason: string
    scope: string
    timestamp: ISO8601
    metadata: object

  Ingestion:
    1. Validate event (idempotency check by event_id)
    2. Append to event store (immutable)
    3. Update sorted set: ZADD leaderboard:{scope} {timestamp} {user_id}
    4. Emit point_awarded event for async processing
    5. Invalidate affected cache slices

ReadModel:
  MaterializedView:
    - scope, user_id, score, rank, first_achieved_at, updated_at
    - rebuilt from event stream via async projection
    - supports multiple indexes per scope

  CacheStrategy:
    hot: top 1000 per scope (Redis ZSET, TTL 30s-5m)
    warm: rank ranges per scope (Redis Hash, TTL 1h)
    cold: full leaderboard in DB (materialized view, refreshed hourly)

Pagination:
  seek-based:
    - use last_seen_score and last_seen_user_id as cursor
    - query: ZRANGEBYSCORE leaderboard:global -inf {last_score} LIMIT {offset} {limit}
    - avoid OFFSET on large sorted sets (O(N) penalty)
  pages:
    - page_size: 20 (default), max 100
    - total_count: ZCARD leaderboard:{scope}
    - has_more: true if more entries exist after current page

Snapshots:
  seasonal:
    - triggered at season end
    - copies current sorted set to snapshot key
    - label: season_{id}_{yyyy-mm-dd}
    - immutable after creation
  historical:
    - weekly snapshots for trend analysis
    - compressed storage for old seasons

RealTimeUpdates:
  WebSocket:
    - subscribe to leaderboard:{scope}:updates
    - receive delta updates (rank change, score change)
    - batch updates: max 1 message per second per client
  Polling:
    - fallback when WebSocket unavailable
    - poll interval: 5s (top 100), 30s (full page)
    - ETag-based conditional requests

Performance:
  getTopN_p99: < 20ms (cached), < 200ms (uncached)
  getUserRank_p99: < 10ms
  rebuild_large_leaderboard: < 5min for 1M users
  concurrent_reads: 10k+ RPS per scope
  cache_hit_rate: > 95% for top-N queries

Best Practices:

  - Use Redis sorted sets for hot leaderboards; fall back to DB for cold
  - Invalidate cache on point events, not on schedule
  - Rebuild stale leaderboards during low-traffic windows
  - Implement circuit breaker for cache failures
  - Monitor leaderboard freshness (max acceptable lag: 30s for real-time)
  - Use connection pooling for high-concurrency read workloads
  - Shard leaderboards by scope when single sorted set exceeds 10M entries
  - Support user opt-out from public leaderboards (privacy)

Anti-Patterns:

  - Full table scan for top-N queries
  - Synchronous leaderboard rebuild on every point event
  - OFFSET-based deep pagination
  - Single global leaderboard without scoping
  - No tie-breaking (random or unstable ordering)
  - Caching without invalidation strategy
  - Recomputing leaderboard from raw events on every request
  - Ignoring timezone in time-window scopes

